Prove the completed migration is behaviorally equivalent and enforce its architecture against regressions. Add dependency/source-contract checks scoped to backend-to-TUI boundaries that reject reintroduction of backend implementation includes, TuiRuntimeStateSnapshot-style transfers, backend construction of frontend-local rendering state and snapshot-bearing action results. Checks must allow documented backend-internal snapshots, frontend-local copies and legitimate neutral action/ordered-interaction contracts; a blanket ban on the word Snapshot is not sufficient. Reconcile every row of the initial ownership inventory with the final canonical owner, mutation publisher, TuiFrontEnd projection, refresh consumer and regression coverage.

Verify deterministic concurrency scenarios: initial registration, update while refreshing, independent output change flags, dependent projections, identical writes, generation coherence, rapid session replacement, stale async completion, pending decisions during cancellation and clean shutdown without notifying destroyed frontends. Verify no render path reads backend files, recomputes canonical statistics or reaches Session/coordinator objects. Capture evidence that /exit no longer causes redundant statistics publication and that model/context changes refresh independently.

Build the canonical debug-enabled tree using the existing configuration, regenerate print-members if required, run the full credential-free CTest suite and applicable module/debug/API guards, and run the complete opt-in tmux wave plus any added targeted PTY coverage. Record real terminal results and exact rerun commands for genuine environment blockers; do not count skipped tests as passed. Format changed C++ and run git diff --check. Document the frontend contract, canonical publication ownership, remaining intentionally local snapshot types and how to add another state/projection pair. Completion requires removal of all old transfer paths, not merely passing tests with both implementations installed.
